{"id":"u-b6398f2c-5e39-4b3e-a6c7-34fda518f784","src":"community","title":"Cutting Up Clark Kent Style","author":"Alexander P.","url":"https://www.boostcamp.app/users/ys67zG-cutting-up-clark-kent-style","desc":"This 12-week, 6-day powerbuilding cut is built to keep strength while driving enough hypertrophy volume to hold muscle on lower calories. Every session starts with one moderately heavy primary lift that ramps into a hard 6-8 rep top set, followed by one dumbbell or machine cluster movement to accumulate 30-50 or 20-40 total reps with joint-friendlier loading. The split keeps Bench Press, Squat, Deadlift, and Overhead Press in weekly rotation, utilizes 4-week waves, powerbuilding frequency, controlled pyramids, and  finishes with a pump bias on the back half of sessions. Progress is managed by small weekly load jumps only when reps and form are earned. Wave 1 builds work capacity, Wave 2 adds cluster volume and accessory sets, and Wave 3 pushes the highest density while still avoiding low-rep grinding that is harder to recover from in a caloric deficit.\n6 days/week: Push, Legs A (quad), Pull, Upper, Legs B (ham/glute), Arms\nEvery session starts with 1 primary lift ramping to a 6-8 rep top set. Use 12/10/8/6-8 on all primary lifts except Deadlift, which uses 10/8/6/6-8 to better manage fatigue while cutting. Weight is only increased to 10/8/6/6-8 and 8/6/4/4-6 on the last wave.\nFor the cluster sets: start with 70% of your current 10RM. Accumulate reps with 10-20 second mini-rests. Add 5 lb when you hit the minimum total reps with clean form. Make sure to keep a note of your cluster set, for ex. 20-10-5 or 20-4-3-2 so you can better adjust week by week.\nWeeks 1-4: 1 x 30-50 cluster set. Base accessory volume.\nWeeks 5-8: 2 x 30-50 cluster sets. Add accessory sets on most days.\nWeeks 9-12: 3 x 20-40 cluster sets. Highest density wave with a higher target weight.\nKeep 1-2 reps in reserve on most work, avoid failed reps, and prioritize exercise execution over load jumps. \nMain lifts 2.5-4 min, cluster mini-rests 10-20 sec, accessory compounds 75-150 sec, isolations 45-75 sec.","level":["Intermediate"],"goals":["Athletics","Muscle","Strength"],"equipment":["Full Gym"],"minutes":70,"joins":5,"rate":0,"rateCount":0,"updated":"2026-10-18T03:34:11.687Z","variations":[{"name":"default","days":["Push","Legs A","Pull","Upper","Legs B","Arms"],"weeks":[[{"ex":[{"n":"Bench Press (Barbell)","sets":[{"r":12},{"r":10},{"r":8},{"lo":6,"hi":8}]},{"n":"Incline Bench Press (Dumbbell)","sets":[{"lo":30,"hi":50}],"note":"Use 70% of current 10RM in week 1. Accumulate total reps across mini-sets. Add 5 lb when minimum total reps are hit."},{"n":"Shoulder Press (Machine)","sets":[{"lo":8,"hi":10,"x":3}]},{"ss":[{"n":"Chest Fly (Cable)","sets":[{"lo":12,"hi":15,"x":3}]},{"n":"Lateral Raise (Cable)","sets":[{"lo":12,"hi":20,"x":3}]}]},{"n":"Tricep Rope Push Down (Cable)","sets":[{"lo":10,"hi":15,"x":3}]},{"n":"Overhead Tricep Extension (Cable)","sets":[{"lo":12,"hi":15,"x":2}]}]},{"ex":[{"n":"Squat (Barbell)","sets":[{"r":12},{"r":10},{"r":8},{"lo":6,"hi":8}]},{"n":"Leg Press","sets":[{"lo":30,"hi":50}],"note":"Use 70% of current 10RM in week 1. Accumulate total reps across mini-sets. Add 25 lb when minimum total reps are hit."},{"n":"Leg Extension","sets":[{"lo":12,"hi":15,"x":3}]},{"n":"Standing Calf Raise","sets":[{"lo":10,"hi":15,"x":4}]},{"n":"Walking Lunge (Dumbbell)","sets":[{"lo":10,"hi":12,"x":2}]}]},{"ex":[{"n":"Barbell Row","sets":[{"r":12},{"r":10},{"r":8},{"lo":6,"hi":8}]},{"n":"Pull-Up (Weighted)","sets":[{"lo":6,"hi":10,"x":3}]},{"n":"Chest Supported Row (Machine)","sets":[{"lo":30,"hi":50}],"note":"Use 70% of current 10RM in week 1. Accumulate total reps across mini-sets. Add 10 lb when minimum total reps are hit."},{"ss":[{"n":"Lat Pulldown","sets":[{"lo":10,"hi":12,"x":2}]},{"n":"Straight Arm Pulldown","sets":[{"lo":10,"hi":15,"x":2}]}]},{"n":"Rear Delt Fly (Machine)","sets":[{"lo":15,"hi":20,"x":3}]},{"n":"Incline Curl (Dumb